.TH DANBY-TWOCAPITAL 1
.SH NAME
danby-twocapital \- one-sector growth with two capital stocks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/twocapital
.SH MODEL
Y=A K1^alpha K2^(1-alpha);
K1'=s1Y-d1K1;
K2'=s2Y-d2K2.
.PP
Output Y uses a constant-returns Cobb-Douglas combination of two complementary
capital stocks.  Separate investment and depreciation rates reveal balanced
growth, bottlenecks, and changes in capital composition.
.SH DISPLAY
Both capital histories and current stocks are displayed.  The controls vary
productivity, output share, both investment fractions, and both depreciation
rates.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag either capital bar.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/twocapital.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/twocapital.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR populationmodel (2),
.IR numerics (2)
